Thanks for collecting the original study and follow-up evaluations. The note about which model sizes can do this is closely related to our paper, *Language Models Can Rewrite Their Own Weights*. MIT's study used a frontier model to edit a smaller Qwen. In our experiment, Qwen3.5-27B used tool feedback to propose and check edits to its own weights. One retained edit improved accuracy by 6.6 percentage points on 490 separate math problems. The smaller checkpoints we tested did not improve, so the result is specific to the 27B setup.

[Preprint](

{% raw %}
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.21885)
{% endraw %}

